eads the light out.","explanation":"Misconception: confuses blocking with spreading; an opaque object blocks light rather than scattering it over the whole screen."},{"id":"around_edges","text":"Only around the edges of the object, because light curves around it.","explanation":"Misconception: assumes light bends around objects; light travels in straight lines and does not curve around an opaque object."}],"presentation":"text","correct_option_id":"opposite_side"},"prompt":"A lamp shines on an opaque object standing in front of a screen. Where does the shadow appear on the screen, and why?","contract":{"id":"ix-check-b1-choice","kind":"choice","config":{"options":[{"id":"opposite_side","text":"On the far side of the object from the lamp, because the opaque object blocks the light travelling in straight lines.","explanation":"Correct: light travels in straight lines from the lamp, the opaque object blocks it, and the shadow is the blocked-light region on the screen on the side opposite the lamp."},{"id":"same_side","text":"On the same side of the object as the lamp, because light bounces back from the object.","explanation":"Misconception: treats the shadow as reflected light returning toward the lamp, instead of light being blocked on the far side."},{"id":"all_screen","text":"Across the whole screen, because the object spreads the light out.","explanation":"Misconception: confuses blocking with spreading; an opaque object blocks light rather than scattering it over the whole screen."},{"id":"around_edges","text":"Only around the edges of the object, because light curves around it.","explanation":"Misconception: assumes light bends around objects; light travels in straight lines and does not curve around an opaque object."}],"presentation":"text","correct_option_id":"opposite_side"},"prompt":"A lamp shines on an opaque object standing in front of a screen. Where does the shadow appear on the screen, and why?","feedback":{"correct":"Correct. The lamp emits light that